title: Proposition 19
---
order: 19
---
short_label: XI.19
---
sections:

#### prop_section ####
kind: proposition
----
statement: If two planes which cut one another are at right angles to any plane, then their intersection is also at right angles to the same plane.
----
proof:

Let the two planes {AB|planeAB} and {BC|planeBC} be at right angles to the plane of reference, and let *BC* be their intersection.

I say that {BD|DB} is at right angles to the plane of reference.

<figure class="diagram">
<canvas id="canvas_0" width="290" height="270" tabindex="0"></canvas>
